{"section":{"id":"cet4-2025-12-set2-news-report-1","examId":"cet4-2025-12-set2","title":"新闻 1","kind":"新闻","start":42.1,"end":129.5,"preview":"Customs and Border Protection officials are seeing a rise in people illegally bringing eggs from Mexico into border states such as Texas.","lines":[{"start":42.1,"end":52.6,"text":"Customs and Border Protection officials are seeing a rise in people illegally bringing eggs from Mexico into border states such as Texas."},{"start":52.6,"end":59.7,"text":"The U.S. average price for a dozen large eggs last month hit $4.25."},{"start":59.7,"end":67.1,"text":"That's more than double their $1.78 price in December 2023."},{"start":67.1,"end":73.2,"text":"Meanwhile, 30 eggs in Mexico sell for just $3.40."},{"start":73.2,"end":78.9,"text":"Those bringing eggs into the U.S. risk fines of up to $10,000."},{"start":78.9,"end":83.4,"text":"But officials say they usually seize and destroy the eggs."},{"start":83.4,"end":87.5,"text":"They also impose a $300 penalty."},{"start":87.5,"end":92.5,"text":"The Department of Agriculture banned eggs from Mexico in 2012."},{"start":92.5,"end":96.2,"text":"This was due to the risk of bird flu."},{"start":96.2,"end":103.6,"text":"Officials said most people arriving at international borders with eggs are truthful about their purchases."},{"start":103.6,"end":108.1,"text":"They simply don't know bringing eggs is not allowed."},{"start":108.1,"end":120,"text":"\"Generally, the items are declared during the first inspection. Then the person can abandon the eggs without consequence,\" a Customs and Border Protection spokesperson said."},{"start":120,"end":129.5,"text":"Even so, there have been a very small number of cases recently when authorities discovered eggs during further inspections."}],"audio":"assets/audio/e801a0c80afc3b16a2084023e0813bd3c643f5fddde7fdd5ddf78011f3dc4d65.wav","audioOffset":42.1},"tasks":[{"id":"0-0","text":"Customs and Border Protection officials are seeing a rise in people illegally